---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const p='/equipment/16-04/',manual='https://www.merckmillipore.com/deepweb/assets/sigmaaldrich/product/documents/177/349/milli-q-iq-7000-brochure-en-ms.pdf';
---
<Layout pageTitle="Milli-Q IQ 7000 virtual water ledger" subtitle="" wide={true} description="Read synthetic resistivity telemetry and log a lot-preserving virtual volume transfer."><script is:inline>window.mqModule=import('/equipment/16-04/water.mjs');</script><article class="equipment" id="milliq"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/16-04/">← Equipment 16-04</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Register</a><a href="#mq-ref">References</a><a href="#mq-verify">Verification</a></nav><header class="eq-mast"><p class="eq-meta">16-04 / VIRTUAL FACILITY RESOURCE</p><h2>Move the volume. Keep the lot.</h2><p class="eq-lede">Allocate 100 mL from a synthetic 1 L lot. Check that the supply drops to 900 mL, the empty bottle gains 100 mL, and the same quality record travels with it.</p></header>
<div class="cols"><section><p class="eq-meta">01 / INSTRUMENT</p><h3>Milli-Q IQ 7000 with one Q-POD</h3><div id="mq-view" aria-label="Metric production unit, dispenser and virtual receiving bottle"></div><small id="mq-model" role="status">Loading metric asset…</small><div class="tools"><button id="mq-all">Whole system</button><button id="mq-pod">Q-POD and bottle</button><button id="mq-cab">Production cabinet</button><button id="mq-cut">Show decorative cassette cutaway</button></div><p>Drag to orbit, scroll or pinch to zoom. The white cabinet and the Q-POD are scale references. The decorative cassette view is neither a diagram of internal flow nor a replacement procedure.</p></section>
<section><p class="eq-meta">02 / VIRTUAL RESOURCE</p><h3>Record one allocation</h3><div class="fields"><label>Requested volume (mL)<input id="mq-ask" type="number" value="100" min=".001" max="1000" step=".001"/></label><label>Synthetic supply lot<select id="mq-lot"><option value="MQ-V001">MQ-V001 · 18.2 MΩ·cm</option><option value="MQ-V002">MQ-V002 · 10 MΩ·cm</option></select></label></div><div class="tools"><button id="mq-run" class="run">Allocate virtual volume</button><button id="mq-bottle">Unseat virtual bottle</button><button id="mq-new">New virtual bottle</button><button id="mq-reset">Reset virtual example</button></div><p id="mq-status" role="status">Synthetic telemetry ready.</p><p>The destination capacity is 250 mL. Changing lot loads another 1 L virtual test record; it does not mix the prior bottle or delete its event history. Choose an empty virtual bottle to accept a different lot.</p></section></div>
<section><p class="eq-meta">03 / TELEMETRY &amp; PROVENANCE</p><h3>Capacity, quantity and lot</h3><p id="mq-result" aria-live="polite"></p><p id="mq-quality"></p><div class="over"><table><thead><tr><th>Event</th><th>Bottle ID</th><th>Source lot</th><th>Credited mL</th><th>Remaining mL</th></tr></thead><tbody id="mq-events"></tbody></table></div><div class="tools"><button id="mq-save">Export virtual ledger JSON</button><a href={p+'example-ledger.json'}>Example ledger</a></div></section>
<section id="mq-ref"><p class="eq-meta">04 / DOCUMENTED EXTERIOR</p><h3>One bench-mounted ZIQ7000T0C/Q-POD pair</h3><p>Exterior follows the <a href={manual+'#page=1'}>MilliporeSigma brochure cover photo</a>, with the compact white production housing, external Q-POD pole and touchscreen. The published <a href={manual+'#page=19'}>Appendix 2</a> gives width × depth × height 265 × 350 × 498 mm. <a href={manual+'#page=20'}>Appendix 3</a> gives a 211 × 270 mm base, 53 mm base height and 792 mm total Q-POD height. Seven asset bounds checked against these values. The stylized screen, local housing details, cable trajectory, bottle and decorative cutaway are original approximations. No vendor photographs are republished.</p><div class="tools"><a href={p+'build-model.py'} download>Editable Blender source</a><a href={p+'iq7000.glb'} download>Download GLB</a><a href={p+'xr.json'}>Geometry checks and VR targets</a><a href={p+'water.mjs'}>State and ledger model</a></div></section>
<section id="mq-verify"><p class="eq-meta">05 / VERIFICATION &amp; LIMITS</p><h3>Conservation and reciprocal units</h3><p>Volumes are integer microlitres internally. Each event debits the virtual source and credits the destination atomically. A mounted bottle and sufficient destination and supply are required. Different lot IDs cannot mix in this virtual ledger. The conductivity in µS/cm equals the reciprocal of resistivity in MΩ·cm at the same temperature; no temperature correction or TOC inference is performed.</p><div class="over"><table><thead><tr><th>Independent reference</th><th>Expected</th><th>Computed</th><th>Criterion</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>1,000 → 100 mL event</th><td>900 mL remaining, 100 mL bottle, MQ-V001</td><td>900 / 100 / MQ-V001</td><td>Exact</td></tr><tr><th>10 MΩ·cm</th><td>0.1 µS/cm at 25 °C</td><td>0.1 µS/cm at 25 °C</td><td>Exact</td></tr><tr><th>251 mL into empty 250 mL bottle</th><td>Reject with unchanged inventory</td><td>Rejected</td><td>Exact</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p><code>bts.virtual-water-ledger.v1</code> exports source and destination IDs, capacity/current volume in mL, lot-tagged telemetry, state revision and every event. These are synthetic examples, not measurements, water-quality certification, a water-system hardware procedure, or biological use instructions. The asset is metric and VR-action ready; no physical headset test is claimed.</p></section>
</article></Layout><script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/16-04/client.mjs';</script><style is:global>
#milliq .cols,#milliq .fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.14fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:.8rem}#milliq section{border:1px solid var(--border);padding:1rem;margin:.8rem 0;min-width:0}#milliq .cols section{margin:0}#milliq .eq-meta{margin:0}#milliq h3{margin:.3rem 0 .6rem;font-size:1.5rem}#milliq .tools{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:.45rem;margin:.65rem 0}#milliq label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-width:0}#milliq input,#milliq select,#milliq button{min-height:40px;padding:.35rem;max-width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;font:inherit;border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--panel,transparent);color:var(--text)}#milliq button{cursor:pointer}#milliq button.run{background:#335e58;color:white}#mq-view{height:clamp(268px,32vw,420px);background:#273538}#mq-view canvas{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;touch-action:none}#milliq .over{overflow:auto}#milliq table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}#milliq th,#milliq td{text-align:left;padding:.42rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}#mq-result{font-weight:bold}#milliq code{overflow-wrap:anywhere}@media(max-width:760px){#milliq .cols{grid-template-columns:1fr}#milliq section{padding:.68rem}}
</style>
